398.el5 before and after execution and restart. node1 runs the CentOS-packaged MySQL 5.0.95 server.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","cmd-9835443a22634330","cmd-fc239f861d3946c4"]}],"confidence":0.94,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.7,"summary":"The final system is functional, but execution included several avoidable mutations. cmd-93895972453b4569 wrote an empty bind-address and stopped MySQL; cmd-20160fe9a4114e19 corrected it. Failed SCP attempts cmd-08f3c24ac3b94a78 and cmd-3557d1acfc0742ec created temporary private-key and credential files that did not contribute to the solution; cmd-e471e4310c6943b7 later removed them. cmd-c5aad34d243049b9 may have appended a non-contributing cluster key to node2's authorized_keys, but the conditional command output does not establish whether it changed the file or whether anything remained. Package commands cmd-1a75bfd70fd94b4e and cmd-5d651389e3ef4489 retained redundant i386 MySQL packages alongside x86_64 packages. The eventual credential transfer used a plaintext HTTP listener bound to all interfaces, though its firewall admission was limited to node2 and cmd-e471e4310c6943b7 removed it. Required restart commands cmd-4b34eff24e7a48ff and cmd-2d21eeb24f324cbe left mysql-benchmark-reboot.log files on both nodes. Raw password helper files created by cmd-b63e13bcd607423e had a setup role and restrictive permissions, but their final removal was not demonstrated.","evidence_ids":["cmd-93895972453b4569","cmd-20160fe9a4114e19","cmd-08f3c24ac3b94a78","cmd-c5aad34d243049b9","cmd-3557d1acfc0742ec","cmd-cfa3d0cc5e9b401a","cmd-e471e4310c6943b7","cmd-1a75bfd70fd94b4e","cmd-5d651389e3ef4489","cmd-b63e13bcd607423e","cmd-4b34eff24e7a48ff","cmd-2d21eeb24f324cbe","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All five material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, changed post-restart identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, data, credentials, and access behavior. Operational hygiene is reduced by a corrected MySQL outage, two failed credential-transfer attempts, redundant packages, bounded plaintext credential transfer, and retained reboot-log residue.","limitations":["The generic after-executor socket snapshots are empty even though direct executor netstat checks show MySQL listening and node2 successfully connects; the direct behavioral evidence is stronger, but the collector discrepancy lowers confidence slightly.","The lifecycle failed-service probe is unsupported on this legacy non-systemd platform, and its package-health probe invoked unsupported yum syntax, so those global checks do not independently validate service or package consistency.","The evidence does not directly capture the final contents of node2's authorized_keys or whether raw password helper files were removed, limiting certainty about those hygiene concerns."]}
